    {
      "evidence_id": "pdfplumber:abstract",
      "source": "pdf_layout",
      "field": "abstract",
      "raw_text": "Westudynewcandidatesforsymmetriccryptographicprim- itives that leverage alternation between linear functions over Z 2 and Z 3 tosupportfastprotocolsforsecuremultipartycomputation(MPC).This continues the study of weak pseudorandom functions of this kind initi- ated by Boneh et al. (TCC 2018) and Cheon et al. (PKC 2021). We make the following contributions. (cid:129) Candidates.Weproposenewdesignsofsymmetricprimitivesbased on alternating moduli. These include candidate one-way functions, pseudorandom generators, and weak pseudorandom functions. We propose concrete parameters based on cryptanalysis. (cid:129) Protocols. We provide a unified approach for securely evaluating modulus-alternating primitives in different MPC models. For the original candidate of Boneh et al., our protocols obtain at least 2x improvement in all performance measures. We report efficiency benchmarks of an optimized implementation. (cid:129) Applications. We showcase the usefulness of our candidates for a variety of applications. This includes short “Picnic-style” signature schemes, as well as protocols for oblivious pseudorandom functions, hierarchicalkeyderivation,anddistributedkeygenerationforfunc- tion secret sharing.",
